    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's a great question for your paper! The Trans-Pacific Partnership (TPP) had various impacts on different sectors and the working class in the US, and opinions vary widely. Proponents argue that it could have created jobs and led to lower prices on goods, benefiting consumers and potentially supporting domestic workers indirectly. Critics, on the other hand, pointed out potential job losses in certain industries, like manufacturing, due to increased competition, and felt that it did little to address social and economic issues like wages and working conditions directly. A thorough paper would delve into these perspectives, supported by data and analysis.",
